Subject: Port protobuf 34.1's C++ runtime to Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

- InternalMetadata, TaggedAllocationPolicyPtr and TaggedStringPtr kept or
  returned tagged pointers as integers, which drops the capability; keep
  pointer-typed words and tag with pointer arithmetic. ArenaAlign::Ceil
  rounds with pointer arithmetic for the same reason (it went through a
  uintptr_t local, which traps at -O0).
- internal::memswap and MicroString::InternalSwap swapped objects holding
  pointers byte by byte, so protoc trapped after moving a message; swap
  through memcpy, which keeps capabilities.
- Inline assembly (.reloc, empty asm barriers with pointer operands, ror
  with a memory operand, btc, prefetch) is rejected at run time; use the
  portable fallbacks.
- The weak descriptor defaults walk the pb_defaults section through the
  linker's __start_/__stop_ symbols, which Fil-C does not provide.
- upb, the C runtime built alongside, keeps pointers in integer words
  throughout (arena block allocators, upb_value hash entries, tagged
  message and array pointers) and is not ported: its code generators trap,
  so the upb tests are not built. The C++ runtime and protoc do not use it.

PROTOBUF_TAILCALL and the version scripts are handled in ports.nix.
Checked by checks.protobuf / checks.protobuf_33 (tests/protobuf.nix) and
the upstream C++ suite.

